    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="8.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 8.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="8.1" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="314" ed="#liebermann"/>And se ðe ofer þis fals<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#IICn_8-1.lnote.oe.14-2"/> wyrce, þolige þæra handa, þe he þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> fals<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#IICn_8-1.lnote.oe.14-2"/> mid worhte; ⁊ he hi<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#IICn_8-1.lnote.oe.15"/> mid nanon þingon ne gebicge, ne mid golde ne mid seolfre.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="8.1" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="314" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ se ðe ofer ðis fals wyrce, ðolie ðara handa, ðe he þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> fals mid worhte; ⁊ he hí mid nanu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> ðingu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> ne bycge, ne mid golde ne mid seolfre.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="8.1" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="314" ed="#liebermann"/>And se þe ofer þis fals wirce, þolige þara handa, þe he þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> fals mide worhte; ⁊ he hig mid nanan ðingo[<hi rend="italic">n<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_8-1.lnote.oe.2"/></hi>] ne gebicge, ne mid golde ne mid seolfre.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="8.1" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="315" ed="#liebermann"/>Et qui<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#IICn_8-1.lnote.oe.9"/> posthac<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#IICn_8-1.lnote.oe.10"/> falsabit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#IICn_8-1.lnote.oe.11"/>, manum amittat<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#IICn_8-1.lnote.oe.12"/> (perdat), unde fecerit, et nec argento uel<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#IICn_8-1.lnote.oe.13"/> auro uel<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#IICn_8-1.lnote.oe.14"/> ullo modo redimat.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="8.1" corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><pb n="315" ed="#liebermann"/>Et qui dehinc<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IICn_8-1.lnote.oe.5-2"/> inuentus fuerit falsum fecisse, careat manibus, cum quibus falsum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#IICn_8-1.lnote.oe.6-2"/> fecit, et nulla pecunia eas redimat, nec auro nec argento.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="8.1" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="315" ed="#liebermann"/>Quisquis autem posthac falsum fabricauerit, amittat manum, qua illud falsum fabricauit, neque illam quacunque re, siue auro siue argento, redimat.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="8.1" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="178" ed="#robertson"/>⁊ se ðe ofer ðis fals wyrce ðolie ðara handa ðe he þæt fals mid worhte, ⁊ he hí mid nanum ðingum ne bycge, ne mid golde ne mid seolfre.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="258" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And se ðe ofer þis fals wyrce þolige þæra handa þe he þæt fals mid worhte, and he hi mid nanon þingon ne gebicge, ne mid golde ne mid seolfre.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="314" ed="#liebermann"/>Und wer hinfort Fälschung macht, verliere die Hand<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_8-1.lnote.de.1"/>, mit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_8-1.lnote.de.2"/> welcher er die Fälschung gemacht hat; und er löse sie unter keiner Bedingung<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_8-1.lnote.de.3"/>, weder mit Gold noch mit Silber, aus.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_8-1.lnote.de.4"/></ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And whoever makes false coin after this, let him lose the hand with which he made the false coin; and let him not buy it back on any terms, neither with gold nor with silver.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="179" ed="#robertson"/>And he who henceforth coins false money shall forfeit the hand<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IICn_8-1.robnote.n.1"/> with which he made the false money, and he shall not redeem it in any way, either with gold or with silver.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IICn_8-1.whinote.n.1"/><pb n="463" ed="#whitelock"/>And he who after this coins false money is to forfeit the hand with which he coined the false money, and he is not to redeem it at any price, neither with gold nor with silver.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="259" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And henceforth, the person who produces counterfeit money shall forfeit the hands with which he made the false coinage, and he may not save it by any means, neither with gold nor with silver.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="314"><ref target="clause:IIAs_14-1">II As 14.1</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">II As. 14, 1</note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="358"><label>source (roman)</label> <ref target="clause:IIAs_14-1">II As 14.1</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, II Cn 8:1: IV Atr 5:3 } II As 14:1 }</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="358"><label>source (roman)</label> <ref target="clause:IVAtr_5-3">IV Atr 5.3</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, II Cn 8:1: IV Atr 5:3 } II As 14:1 }</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#whitelock" n="463"><label>based on</label> <ref target="clause:IIAs_14-1">II As 14.1</ref> <quote>This is based on II Athelstan, 14.1.</quote></note>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares II As 14.1.; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 315, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
        <note type="translator" source="#rabin-doml">the hands: The Old English þæra handa is ambiguous as to number. Analogous Old English texts use the plural, though Latin versions sometimes use singular and others plural.</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_8-1.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">315</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">post hāc <hi rend="italic">Hk;</hi> post <hi rend="italic">Hr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">post hāc Hk; post Hr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_8-1.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">315</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">arg. s. auro <hi rend="italic">Hr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">arg. s. auro Hr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_8-1.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">315</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt R</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in R</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_8-1.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">315</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">post hanc <hi rend="italic">KRT</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">post hanc KRT</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_8-1.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">315</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">falsificabit <hi rend="italic">K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">falsificabit K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_8-1.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">315</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">am. <hi rend="italic">K;</hi> p. <hi rend="italic">übr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">am. K; p. the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_8-1.lnote.oe.13" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">315</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">nec <hi rend="italic">T;</hi> et <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">nec T; et Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_8-1.lnote.oe.14" n="14" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">315</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">r. uel u. m. <hi rend="italic">K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">r. uel u. m. K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_8-1.lnote.oe.14-2" n="14" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">314</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-se <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-se Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_8-1.lnote.oe.15" n="15" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">314</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">hig m. nānum ðingum <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">hig m. nānum ðingum Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_8-1.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">314</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ðingo <hi rend="italic">A</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ðingo A</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_8-1.lnote.oe.5-2" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">315</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">hinc <hi rend="italic">Lb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">hinc Lb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_8-1.lnote.oe.6-2" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">315</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">fe. fa. <hi rend="italic">Lb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">fe. fa. Lb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_8-1.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">203</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘Hände’ In, Price-Thorpe, Toller 508, falsch laut QC, II As 14, 1, <hi rend="italic">pugnum</hi> Hn 13, 3 aus Q. Spätagsä. kann <hi rend="italic">þæra</hi> Sg. sein. Ebenso <hi rend="italic">u</hi>. 36⁴; ‘Hände’ dagegen 30, 4. 48, 1</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘Hands’ In, Price-Thorpe, Toller 508, wrongly, according to QC, II As 14, 1, <hi rend="italic">pugnum</hi> Hn 13, 3 from Q. In late Anglo-Saxon <hi rend="italic">þæra</hi> can be singular. Likewise <hi rend="italic">below</hi> 36⁴; ‘hands’, on the other hand, 30, 4. 48, 1</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_8-1.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">203</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">mide</hi> A mittelengl.</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">mide</hi> A is Middle English</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_8-1.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">203</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">nicht ‘mit nichts’, sondern Redensart; Toller 1061a 13. 1060b 12</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">not ‘with nothing’, but an idiom; Toller 1061a 13. 1060b 12</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_8-1.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">203</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">S. Gl</hi> busslos 4; Münzfälschung 7</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">See Gl</hi> busslos 4; Münzfälschung 7</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IICn_8-1.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">352</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">I have followed Q, Cons. and Liebermann in taking <hi rend="italic">ðara handa</hi> as singular. Inst., followed by Thorpe, takes it as plural. In view of what follows, however, and of II As. 14, 1, most probably one hand only is meant. In caps. 30, 4; 48, 1 both are to be forfeited.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="IICn_8-1.whinote.n.1" n="1" source="#whitelock"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">463</biblScope></bibl><label>8.1</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">This is based on II Athelstan, 14.1.</seg></note>
      </div>
